.\" ABSD manual page source (mdoc(7)); rendered by scripts/render-man.sh.
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt PRINTF 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm printf
.Nd format and print arguments (sbase)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar format
.Op Ar arg ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is sbase 0.1's
.Nm printf ,
built unpatched for ABSD with the C kit; see
.Xr sbase 7 .
It writes
.Ar format
to standard output, with the backslash escapes and the
.Ql %
conversions
.Pq Ql d i o u x X c s b e E f g G
filled from the arguments in turn; the format is reused while arguments
remain.
It is a program under
.Pa /bin ,
not a shell builtin.
.Sh UNSUPPORTED ON ABSD
Nothing is refused.
Messages begin with the name the program was run as, and their
.Ql strerror
texts are Picolibc's.
Behaviour on ABSD is predicted until the guest qualification
.Pq Xr sbase 7 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when an argument could not be converted (the output is
still written), or on a usage or write error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
absd$ printf '%s=%d\en' size 42
size=42
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr absd-sh 1 ,
.Xr sbase 7
